 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met: three settings, on three different scenes, are confirmed as failing most of the time (S29, S3, S4), against the five the brief asked for. None of the three is the policy rear-ending a car that slows ahead of it.\n\n- **S3 (023b7fcc):** the failures were not the policy's fault. The retimed lead car's box already overlaps the ego while the recording is still being replayed, before the policy takes control.\n- **S4 (096988dd):** this needs 350 ms of planner delay, above the brief's 200 ms limit. In every run the ego drifts left and hits a car in the next lane, and every failure is flagged as a possible simulator artifact.\n- **S29 (19f339ba, 1.5x speed, 200 ms):** the ego brakes hard with no car close ahead, drifts left and clips a car in the left lane.\n\nOn this evidence, retiming the lead car within the brief's limits did not produce the rear-end collisions the brief is after. Single failures at S5 and S30 point the same way (drifting into side traffic), but one run is a hint, not a rate.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, shifting the lead car 1.5 s later at 0.75x speed failed every run. Triage traced every failure to the lead car's box overlapping the ego during log replay, before the policy took over. This is a replay or retiming artifact, not a policy failure and not a rear-end.",
    "settings": [
     "S3"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd, shifting the lead car 2 s earlier at 1.5x speed with 350 ms planner delay failed every run. That delay is above the brief's 200 ms cap. Every failure was the ego steering left against a RIGHT command and side-swiping a car passing in the left lane, not hitting the lead car. Every failure is also flagged as a possible artifact (ego more than 3.5 m off the recorded path).",
    "settings": [
     "S4"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba, 1.5x lead speed with 200 ms delay failed every run. The ego braked hard with no vehicle close ahead, drifted left, and its front-left corner hit a replayed car in the left lane. In one of these runs triage could not say whether the policy was at fault. A single run at +0.5 s, 1.25x and 100 ms failed the same way.",
    "settings": [
     "S29",
     "S30"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The only failure at zero planner delay (096988dd, 1.5 s earlier, 2x speed) was a single run in which the ego drifted into a car passing in the next lane, not into the lead car.",
    "settings": [
